  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `plan_trochoidal_slot` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/trochoid_slot.rs`) now asks the lane planner for the opened bore (`trochoid_bore::bore` with `open: true`, from #1509) when the loop band's half-width `b` is more than the tool radius `r`.\n- Cause: a helix of radius `b` clears only the ring `b +- r`. When `b > r` (a channel wider than twice the tool), the plain bore left a post of radius `b - r` at the start, at full depth. No front arc reached it, and the operation reported OK.\n- When `b <= r`, the slot keeps the plain bore, and the output does not change.\n- The doc comment of `trochoid_bore.rs` now gives the new rule.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1589-troch-slot-open-bore.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `trochoid_wide_channel_leaves_no_post_at_the_start` (motion `tests/trochoid_slot.rs`): D 10, W 26 (b 8, r 5). The rest area in a 2.5 mm disc about the start is 0.000 mm2, and the measured engagement is 78.0 deg (limit 90). With the plain bore forced, the same test fails with 19.72 mm2 standing.\n- `the_opened_bore_leaves_no_post_at_the_lane_start` (motion lib, `adaptive_troch_tests.rs`), extended: the stand-alone slot on the #1509 band (b 4.5 to 5, D 6) leaves less than 0.5 mm2 and holds the engagement limit.\n- `a_slot_band_within_the_tool_radius_keeps_the_plain_bore` (motion lib): W 10 and W 12 with D 6 give a path equal to the plain-bore plan, move for move.\n- The golden `trochoid_slot_small.cl` (app `golden_cl`) does not change.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: motion suites and app suites are green (12.3 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The GUI was not started.\n- No deep-stepdown test on a wide slot. The opened helix has half the tool radius, so it needs more turns. A very deep stepdown can now hit the helix turn cap. That case is refused by name (\"half the tool radius - use a smaller stepdown\").\n- The release-lane heavy suites were not run.\n\nChangelog: Trochoidal slot: a channel wider than twice the tool no longer leaves a post standing at its start; the bore now spirals out to the loop band.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1589\n",
